{
  "name": "the special Netflix inserted at position 14 pairs with nothing",
  "source": {
    "file": "docs/src/content/docs/design/representation.md",
    "test": "section 8.3, Blue Exorcist, the special that broke the offset vote"
  },
  "why": "Netflix lists 26 rows for a 25 episode run because position 14 is \"Runaway Kuro\", a special that aired after the run ended. There is no single shift that makes those 26 rows into these 25: positions 1 to 13 are episodes 1 to 13, positions 15 to 26 are episodes 14 to 25, and position 14 is nobody's episode. The record measured what happens when a number is guessed anyway: \"A title-vote offset scored [[0,12],[1,11]], answered offset 0 by one vote, and put 13 wrong playable urls on the page.\" A wrong play button is worse than a missing one, and nothing downstream can tell the two apart. Netflix publishes no dates here and retranslates its titles, so in this case nothing pairs at all and the Netflix season stays what it is: 26 rows that are not this run.",
