    "at": "2026-09-12",
    "notes": "Every number and every Netflix id is the record's: title 70304252, season 1 of 26 rows against a 25 episode run, position 14 the epid 80005451 \"Runaway Kuro\". The run's own ids are NOT in the record (\"The catalogue run's ids are not in the record\"), so the two run rows carry the placeholder uris the record itself writes for them, anilist:<Blue Exorcist>. The other 25 Netflix positions have no epid in the record either and carry the corpus's <mediaUri>-e<number> convention instead. Neither side is dated here: Netflix publishes none at any level, and the record does not publish anizip's days for this run. The last two episodeApart pairs are the offset the title vote answered: under the piecewise mapping position 15 is episode 14 and position 16 is episode 15, so a page that reads position as number is wrong from 15 on."
